From 9258d0d281bf7172b18f82367a1ee0764aa04edd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zhaosiying12138 <neucszhaopeng2016@163.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 03:14:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] vega: honor the DS-encoding ACC bit for accumulator data
 operands

A live aiter composable-kernel GEMM on gfx950 issues the DS word
0xda784400: ds_read_u16 (OP=0x3c) with ACC (bit 25) set and offset
0x44. tableDecodePrimary mapped the four DS primary-encoding slots
with ACC=1 (0x1B4-0x1B7) to decode_invalid, so the run died with
"Invalid opcode encountered: 0xda784400" although subDecode_OP_DS
keys on the full 8-bit OP field and decodes the word correctly.

Route the four ACC=1 slots to subDecode_OP_DS and give Inst_DS a
general ACC mechanism: dsData0Idx/dsData1Idx/dsVdstIdx add the
wavefront's accumOffset to every DS data operand index when
instData.ACC is set, exactly as V_ACCVGPR_READ/WRITE already map
AGPRs into the unified file. The ADDR operand always names an
architectural VGPR and is never redirected; the reference emulator
types addr as OPR_VGPR while data0/data1/vdst are
OPR_VGPR_OR_ACCVGPR and offsets only the latter by the ACC window.
Every operand-construction site in ds.cc now goes through the
helpers, including the CDNA4 transpose reads, whose packing is
destination-index-agnostic, so their blanket ACC panic is dropped.

Fail closed: a DS ACC operand in a kernel that allocates no AGPRs
(accumOffset unset or beyond the VGPR allocation) is malformed, so
the helper panics with a named reason rather than silently aliasing
low architectural VGPRs. The decoder unit test decodes the live word
and its ACC=0 twin to the same ds_read_u16 opcode.

